---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy" 
  description="Refund & Cancellation Policy — Wugweb project and subscription services."
  hideGlobalSections={true}
>
  <section class="wrap legal">
    <header class="static-head">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>LEGAL & BILLING</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>Refund & Cancellation Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated" data-reveal>Last updated: August 16, 2026</p>
      
      <div class="legal-quick-links" data-reveal>
        <a href="/termsofuse">Terms of Use &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/footer/subscription">Subscription &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p data-reveal>
        This policy explains how cancellations, refunds and subscription changes are handled for Wugweb services. We aim to make our billing and cancellation terms clear before work begins or a subscription is activated.
      </p>

      <!-- 01 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>01 — Our approach</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Refund eligibility depends on the type of service (Project Services or Subscription Services), the stage of work, and the circumstances of the request.
      </p>

      <!-- 02 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>02 — Project services</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        For separately scoped client project engagements, the following rules apply:
      </p>
      <ul data-reveal>
        <li>
          <strong>Before work begins:</strong> If Wugweb has not commenced work and a project is cancelled, refund eligibility will depend on agreed terms, payments committed, and non-refundable third-party costs incurred.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>After work begins:</strong> Payments for work already completed, approved, or delivered are non-refundable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deposits / advance payments:</strong> Advance deposits are non-refundable where they reserve Wugweb capacity or cover work already undertaken.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third-party costs:</strong> Fees paid to platforms, domain registrars, licenses, or production partners are non-refundable once committed on the client's behalf.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 03 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>03 — Wugweb Subscription</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Wugweb Subscription is a recurring monthly service billed in advance for each billing period.
      </p>
      <ul data-reveal>
        <li>
          <strong>Billing:</strong> Your subscription renews automatically at the beginning of each monthly billing cycle unless cancelled before the renewal date.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cancellation:</strong> You may cancel your subscription at any time. Unless otherwise stated in your subscription agreement, cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing cycle. Access remains active for requests until the end of the paid cycle.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 04 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>04 — Subscription refunds</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Subscription fees are non-refundable once a billing period has started because the subscription reserves Wugweb's ongoing capacity for the customer.
      </p>
      <p data-reveal>
        Refunds may be considered under specific circumstances:
      </p>
      <ul data-reveal>
        <li>Duplicate, incorrect, or unauthorized payment charges.</li>
        <li>Payment processor errors or subscription activation failures.</li>
        <li>Wugweb's inability to provide the subscribed service, or where required by law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p data-reveal>
        Refunds are **not** offered because the customer did not submit requests or did not use the subscription during the billing period.
      </p>

      <!-- 05 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>05 — Pausing your subscription</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Our subscription includes a pause facility to fit your workload requirements:
      </p>
      <ul data-reveal>
        <li><strong>Pause starts:</strong> At the end of the current billing period to avoid partial-month scheduling gaps.</li>
        <li><strong>Minimum pause:</strong> 14 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Maximum pause:</strong> 90 days. After 90 days, the subscription will automatically cancel if not resumed.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing during pause:</strong> Recurring billing is suspended.</li>
        <li><strong>Queued work during pause:</strong> Active work stops, and queued requests remain in your backlog until you resume.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 06 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>06 — Failed or overdue payments</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        If a recurring payment fails:
      </p>
      <ul data-reveal>
        <li>We will attempt to re-bill the payment method via Razorpay.</li>
        <li>We will notify you immediately of the payment failure.</li>
        <li>If unresolved within 3 business days, subscription services and active requests are temporarily suspended.</li>
        <li>If unresolved after 7 business days, the subscription will be cancelled.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 07 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>07 — Payment disputes and chargebacks</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        If you believe a charge is incorrect, please contact Wugweb at <a href="mailto:hello@wugweb.com">hello@wugweb.com</a> so we can investigate and resolve the issue. This does not limit any rights you may have under payment rules or law.
      </p>

      <!-- 08 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>08 — Taxes</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Unless expressly stated otherwise, pricing displayed on our website is exclusive of applicable taxes, including GST. Tax charges are detailed during billing confirmation before final payment.
      </p>

      <!-- 09 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>09 — Third-party costs</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Unless expressly included in the applicable subscription terms, third-party software, licences, hosting, domains, APIs, payment processing fees, and advertising media spend are billed separately.
      </p>

      <!-- 10 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>10 — When Wugweb may suspend or cancel services</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Wugweb may suspend or terminate services where reasonably necessary because of non-payment, material breach of the <a href="/termsofuse">Terms of Use</a>, misuse of services, or abusive behavior.
      </p>

      <!-- 11 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>11 — Intellectual property and completed work</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        Ownership and licensing of project deliverables are governed by the applicable agreement, proposal, statement of work or Wugweb <a href="/termsofuse">Terms of Use</a>.
      </p>

      <!-- 12 -->
      <h2 data-reveal>12 — Need help with a payment or refund?</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        If you believe you have been charged incorrectly or believe your situation qualifies for a refund, contact us at:
      </p>
      <p data-reveal>
        <a href="mailto:hello@wugweb.com" class="accent-email">hello@wugweb.com</a>
      </p>

      <!-- 13 — FAQ accordion -->
      <h2 data-reveal>13 — FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq-accordion" id="refund-faq-accordion" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>Can I cancel my Wugweb subscription?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Yes. You can cancel your subscription at any time. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing cycle.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>Will I receive a refund if I cancel?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Subscription fees are generally non-refundable once the current billing period has started, subject to applicable law and exceptions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>What happens to my active request when I cancel?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Your subscription remains active until the end of the current billing period, and we will continue to process your active request during that remaining time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>Can I pause my subscription?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Yes, where the pause option is available under your subscription terms. You can pause at the end of the billing period for up to 90 days.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>What happens if my payment fails?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>We will attempt to re-bill. If unresolved within 3 business days, services are suspended. After 7 business days, the subscription cancels.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>Are project deposits refundable?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Refund eligibility depends on the project agreement, work completed, committed costs, and circumstances of cancellation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>Are third-party costs refundable?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Generally, third-party costs that Wugweb has already committed or paid (licenses, hosting, API costs) are non-refundable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-header">
            <span>How do I request a refund?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-panel">
            <p>Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@wugweb.com">hello@wugweb.com</a> with the relevant billing or invoice information.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: var(--space-section-xl);
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .static-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    padding-bottom: var(--p-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--gap-10);
  }

  .legal h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-h1);
    margin-block: var(--gap-3) var(--gap-2);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fluid-label);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .legal-quick-links {
    margin-top: var(--gap-4);
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--gap-6);
  }

  .legal-quick-links a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fluid-caption);
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .legal-quick-links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--fluid-h3);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    margin-top: var(--gap-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--gap-4);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    padding-top: var(--p-6);
  }

  .legal-body p, .legal-body li {
    font-size: var(--fluid-body-md);
    line-height: var(--core-line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--gap-4);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--gap-6);
    padding-left: var(--p-5);
  }

  .legal-body li {
    margin-bottom: var(--gap-2);
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .legal-body a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .accent-email {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fluid-body-md);
    color: var(--color-accent-primary) !important;
  }

  /* Accordion styles */
  .faq-accordion {
    margin-top: var(--gap-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .faq-header {
    width: 100%;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--p-5) 0;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--fluid-body-lg);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .faq-header:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
  }

  .faq-icon {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    transition: transform 0.3s;
  }

  .faq-panel {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s cubic-bezier(0, 1, 0, 1);
  }

  .faq-panel p {
    padding-bottom: var(--p-5);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .faq-item.active .faq-panel {
    max-height: 1000px;
    transition: max-height 0.3s cubic-bezier(1, 0, 1, 0);
  }

  .faq-item.active .faq-icon {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Setup accordion
  const faqContainer = document.getElementById('refund-faq-accordion');
  if (faqContainer) {
    const items = faqContainer.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');
    items.forEach(item => {
      const header = item.querySelector('.faq-header');
      if (header) {
        header.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const isActive = item.classList.contains('active');
          items.forEach(i => i.classList.remove('active'));
          if (!isActive) {
            item.classList.add('active');
          }
        });
      }
    });
  }
</script>
